steps.body:
Sometimes you need to know which *round* reached a cell, such as the minute a fire got there. Process the queue one level at a time: before each round, record how many items are waiting, then handle exactly that many.

```javascript harness
const queue = [[0, 0], [2, 3]]; // two fire sources
let head = 0;
{{code}}
console.log(`Processed ${head} cells`);
```

```javascript
while (head < queue.length) {
  const size = queue.length - head;
  for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) {
    const [r, c] = queue[head++];
    // push neighbors for the next round
  }
}
```

Cells pushed during a round land after those `size` items, so they wait for the next round. Each round is one minute.

**Multi-source BFS** starts from every source at once: push all of them before the loop. They spread together, and each cell is reached from its nearest source.

Count a minute only when a round added new cells (`head < queue.length` after the round). Otherwise the final round, which spreads nothing, counts one too many. You can mark visited by changing the grid itself (`grid[nr][nc] = "F"`). When BFS finishes, scan the grid: any cell still unmarked was never reached. `grid.flat()` joins the rows into one array, so `grid.flat().filter((cell) => cell === ".").length` counts them.

example.code:
const input = require("fs").readFileSync(0, "utf8");
const grid = input.trim().split("\n").map((line) => line.trim().split(""));
const directions = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]];

function spreadFire(grid) {
  const rows = grid.length;
  const cols = grid[0].length;
  const queue = [];
  for (let r = 0; r < rows; r++) {
    for (let c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
      if (grid[r][c] === "F") {
        queue.push([r, c]);
      }
    }
  }
  let head = 0;
  let minutes = 0;
  while (head < queue.length) {
    const size = queue.length - head;
    for (let i = 0; i < size; i++) {
      const [r, c] = queue[head++];
      for (const [dr, dc] of directions) {
        const nr = r + dr;
        const nc = c + dc;
        if (nr >= 0 && nr < rows && nc >= 0 && nc < cols && grid[nr][nc] === ".") {
          grid[nr][nc] = "F";
          queue.push([nr, nc]);
        }
      }
    }
    if (head < queue.length) {
      minutes++;
    }
  }
  const unburned = grid.flat().filter((cell) => cell === ".").length;
  return [minutes, unburned];
}

const [minutes, unburned] = spreadFire(grid);
console.log(`Minutes: ${minutes}`);
console.log(`Unburned: ${unburned}`);

